# The STL mesher (user request 2026-10-23): an STL's path typed in, the part read (closed, split into boundaries by
# angle), meshed with snappyHexMesh from the STAR-CCM+-style settings, with prism layers, and checked.
budget p95 40 max 400
open $SB/ws/cavity
shell zcat "${FOAM_TUTORIALS:-/usr/lib/openfoam/openfoam2606/tutorials}/resources/geometry/flange.stl.gz" > ../flange.stl
click nav:mesh
wait-until page Mesh
click text:STL mesher
wait 5
assert text Start with the part
click stl-path
enter $SB/ws/flange.stl
wait 10
assert text 6468 triangles
assert text Closed (watertight)
assert text 24 boundaries
assert file mesher/mesher.ini
note the flow: Geometry > Flow > Boundaries > Mesh settings > Generate
click stl-next
wait 3
click stl-next
wait 3
click stl-next
wait 3
assert text Cell size
click stl-next
wait 3
note the cavity seed comes meshed (blockMesh, no mesher signature): Generate shows the estimate, not "Not generated yet"
assert text (a rough estimate)
click stl-gen
wait-until job running timeout 20
wait-until job finished timeout 900
assert log log.checkMesh Mesh OK.
assert log constant/polyMesh/boundary patch1_1
assert log system/snappyHexMeshDict nSurfaceLayers 3
assert file system/blockMeshDict.orig
screenshot $OUT/stl_mesher.png
